CAUSAL-CREDIT / EVIDENCE FRONTIER
Current supported synthetic sequence includes:

dg1a-aru10-local-disturbance-subspace-poc.ice

Key result:
action orthogonalization is conditional.

Low action contamination:
full disturbance prediction can be better.

High contamination:
down-weighting action-responsive reference components improves causal-sign accuracy.

dg1a-aru11-adaptive-causal-baseline-gating-audit.ice

Key result:
locally selecting between full and action-orthogonalized baselines improves causal-sign fidelity.

Defer introduces a real:
credit fidelity
vs
adaptation throughput
tradeoff.

dg1a-aru12-confidence-weighted-plasticity-audit.ice

Key result:
confidence is best used as a plasticity modulator,
not as causal certainty.

Continuous weighting can outperform both unconditional update and hard defer.

dg1a-aru13-budgeted-active-evidence-audit.ice

Key result:
evidence is a real adaptive resource.

At the primary working point,
a token-bucket policy retained near-unbounded recovery while materially reducing probe use.

Stable periods should conserve adaptive capacity.

Surprise should recruit it.

dg1a-aru14-value-of-information-urgency-audit.ice

Key result:
uncertainty alone does not encode functional value.

At the same mean evidence budget,
synthetic value-of-information allocation reduced weighted wrong-decision cost relative to both:
- equal allocation;
- stakes-only allocation.

The conceptual controller should estimate:

EXPECTED FUNCTIONAL IMPROVEMENT
PER
ADAPTIVE RESOURCE SPENT

subject to deadline / urgency.

This is a value principle,
not yet a demonstrated local learned implementation.

