H6 PRINCIPLE
Do not force:

SHOULD I EXPRESS THIS MEMORY NOW?

and

SHOULD I ERASE / REWRITE THIS MEMORY?

to share one time constant.

Preferred ordering:

contradiction
->
fast inherited-expression suppression
->
fast phenotype adaptation
->
slow rewrite only after persistent stale-prior evidence.

CONTEXT / PROVENANCE FRONTIER
The live branch retains overlapping context/provenance sequences.

Important established principles remain:

COPIES ARE NOT REDUNDANCY.

PHYSICAL CELL COUNT IS NOT SOURCE INDEPENDENCE.

SOURCE EVIDENCE NEEDS PROVENANCE ACROSS RELAYING.

INDEPENDENCE MUST BE EARNED FROM EVIDENCE,
NOT ASSIGNED MERELY BECAUSE A NEW CELL EXISTS.

Compressed idempotent source sketches can preserve much of exact-source voting value while avoiding relay-copy inflation.

However:

CONSENSUS CANNOT MANUFACTURE INDEPENDENCE.

Common-mode correlated sensor errors can make many agreeing sources confidently wrong.

This remains an open context-confidence problem.

A supplemental sensor-diversity/common-mode audit path was created and then removed as superseded before this seal.

Do not infer current authority from that removed path.

Use currently present filenames and live commit history.

